      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes a mechanism for protecting file writes against failure. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state into an in-memory write journal. This records either:\n- The file\u0027s previous content (if it existed), or\n- The fact that it did not exist\n\n**Rollback capability**: If the agent run fails \u2014 whether from exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes \u2014 the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order. This restores previous content for files that existed and deletes any newly created files.\n\n**Transaction semantics**: This approach provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Query agent note**: The Query agent (the agent you\u0027re interacting with now) never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
